isRegularMap -- whether a map to projective space is regular
************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        b = isRegularMap(f)
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note ring map: (Macaulay2Doc)RingMap,, a ring map corresponding
        to a rational map of projective varieties
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Verbosity => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value 0, if 0
        then silence the function, if 1 then generate informative output which
        can be used to adjust strategies, if > 1 then generate a detailed
        description of the execution
  * Outputs:
      * b, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, 

Description
===========

This function runs baseLocusOfMap(f) and checks whether the ideal defining the
base locus is the whole ring.

+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : P5 = QQ[a..f];                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : P2 = QQ[x,y,z];                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : M = matrix{{a,b,c},{d,e,f}};                    |
|                                                     |
|              2       3                              |
|o3 : Matrix P5  <-- P5                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : blowUpSubvar = P5/(minors(2, M) + ideal(b - d));|
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : f = map(blowUpSubvar, P2, {a, b, c});           |
|                                                     |
|o5 : RingMap blowUpSubvar <-- P2                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : isRegularMap(f)                                 |
|                                                     |
|o6 = true                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------+

