mapOntoImage -- the induced map from a variety to the closure of its image under a rational map
***********************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        h = mapOntoImage(f)
        psi = mapOntoImage(phi)
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note ring map: (Macaulay2Doc)RingMap,, the ring map corresponding
        to a rational map $\phi$ of projective varieties
      * phi, an instance of the type *note RationalMapping: RationalMapping,, a
        rational map $\phi$ of projective varieties
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * QuickRank => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default
        value true, whether to compute rank via the package *note FastMinors:
        (FastMinors)Top,
  * Outputs:
      * h, a *note ring map: (Macaulay2Doc)RingMap,, the map of rings
        corresponding to $X \to \overline{\phi(X)}$.
      * psi, an instance of the type *note RationalMapping: RationalMapping,,
        the rational map

Description
===========

Given $f : X \to Y$ mapOntoImage returns $X \to \overline{\phi(X)}$.
Alternately, given $f: S \to R$, mapOntoImage just returns $S/(kernel f) \to
R$.  mapOntoImage first computes whether the kernel is $0$ without calling
*note ker: (Macaulay2Doc)kernel_lpRingMap_rp,, which can have speed advantages.

+--------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y];                                 |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : S = QQ[a,b,c];                               |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : f = map(R, S, {x^2, x*y, y^2});              |
|                                                  |
|o3 : RingMap R <-- S                              |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : mapOntoImage(f)                              |
|                                                  |
|                 S       2        2               |
|o4 = map (R, --------, {x , x*y, y })             |
|              2                                   |
|             b  - a*c                             |
|                                                  |
|                       S                          |
|o4 : RingMap R <-- --------                       |
|                    2                             |
|                   b  - a*c                       |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : phi = rationalMapping f                      |
|                                                  |
|                               2        2         |
|o5 = Proj R - - - > Proj S   {x , x*y, y }        |
|                                                  |
|o5 : RationalMapping                              |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : mapOntoImage(phi)                            |
|                                                  |
|                        /    S   \     2        2 |
|o6 = Proj R - - - > Proj|--------|   {x , x*y, y }|
|                        | 2      |                |
|                        \b  - a*c/                |
|                                                  |
|o6 : RationalMapping                              |
+--------------------------------------------------+

