MinorsLimit -- an option to limit the number of random minors computed
**********************************************************************

Description
===========

One of the ways to invert a map is to find a nonzero minor of a variant of the
jacobianDualMatrix. This function controls how many minors (heuristically
chosen via *note FastMinors: (FastMinors)Top,) to check before switching to
another strategy (involving computing a syzygy). Setting it to zero will mean
no minors are checked. If it is left as null (the default), these functions
will determine a value using a heuristic that depends on the varieties
involved.

See also
========

  * *note inverseOfMap: inverseOfMap, -- inverse of a birational map between
    projective varieties

Functions with optional argument named MinorsLimit:
===================================================

  * "inverseOfMap(...,MinorsLimit=>...)" -- see *note inverseOfMap:
    inverseOfMap, -- inverse of a birational map between projective varieties
  * "isBirationalMap(...,MinorsLimit=>...)" -- see *note isBirationalMap:
    isBirationalMap, -- whether a map between projective varieties is
    birational
  * "isBirationalOntoImage(...,MinorsLimit=>...)" -- see *note
    isBirationalOntoImage: isBirationalOntoImage, -- whether a map between
    projective varieties is birational onto its image
  * "isEmbedding(...,MinorsLimit=>...)" -- see *note isEmbedding: isEmbedding,
    -- whether a rational map of projective varieties is a closed embedding
  * "sourceInversionFactor(...,MinorsLimit=>...)" -- see *note
    sourceInversionFactor: sourceInversionFactor, -- computes the common factor
    among the components of the composition of the inverse map and the original
    map

