ReesStrategy -- a strategy for determining whether a map is birational and computing its inverse
************************************************************************************************

Description
===========

ReesStrategy is a valid value for the Strategy Option for inverseOfMap,
isBirationalMap, and isEmbedding. By choosing Strategy=>ReesStrategy, the ideal
of definition of the Rees algebra is computed by the known elimination
technique. This technique is described in Proposition 1.5 on page 21 in the
book

  * Vasconcelos, Wolmer.  Integral closure. Springer Monographs in Mathematics.
    Springer-Verlag, Berlin,2005. xii+519 pp.

See also
========

  * *note SaturationStrategy: SaturationStrategy, -- a strategy for determining
    whether a map is birational and computing its inverse
  * *note SimisStrategy: SimisStrategy, -- a strategy for determining whether a
    map is birational and computing its inverse
  * *note HybridStrategy: HybridStrategy, -- A strategy for determining whether
    a map is birational and computing its inverse

