SaturationStrategy -- a strategy for determining whether a map is birational and computing its inverse
******************************************************************************************************

Description
===========

SaturationStrategy is a valid value for the Strategy Option for inverseOfMap,
isBirationalMap, and isEmbedding. By choosing Strategy=>SaturationStrategy, the
equations of the ideal of definition of the Rees algebra are generated by
saturating the ideal of definition of the symmetric algebra into a non-zero
element. Notice that in this package (and in particular, in this Strategy
option) the rings are assumed to be integral domains. This Strategy appears to
be slower in some examples.

See also
========

  * *note ReesStrategy: ReesStrategy, -- a strategy for determining whether a
    map is birational and computing its inverse
  * *note SimisStrategy: SimisStrategy, -- a strategy for determining whether a
    map is birational and computing its inverse
  * *note HybridStrategy: HybridStrategy, -- A strategy for determining whether
    a map is birational and computing its inverse

