File: RationalMaps.info, Node: SimisStrategy, Next: source_lpRationalMapping_rp, Prev: SaturationStrategy, Up: Top

SimisStrategy -- a strategy for determining whether a map is birational and computing its inverse
*************************************************************************************************

Description
===========

SimisStrategy is a valid value for the Strategy Option of inverseOfMap,
isBirationalMap, and isEmbedding. Considering the bigraded structure of the
equations of the ideal of definition of a Rees algebra, SimisStrategy looks for
all Gröbner bases where the degree is (1, n) for some natural number n. The
advantage of this restriction is that this part of the Rees ideal is enough to
decide birationality and to compute the inverse map; this strategy reduces
computation time. A disadvantage of this Strategy is that if the given map is
not birational this Strategy may never end because the jacobianDualMatrix will
not attain its maximum rank. To circumvent this problem we implemented
HybridStrategy.

See also
========

  * *note ReesStrategy: ReesStrategy, -- a strategy for determining whether a
    map is birational and computing its inverse
  * *note SaturationStrategy: SaturationStrategy, -- a strategy for determining
    whether a map is birational and computing its inverse
  * *note HybridStrategy: HybridStrategy, -- A strategy for determining whether
    a map is birational and computing its inverse

For the programmer
==================

The object *note SimisStrategy: SimisStrategy, is a *note symbol:
(Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,.

