File: RationalMaps.info, Node: sourceInversionFactor, Prev: source_lpRationalMapping_rp, Up: Top

sourceInversionFactor -- computes the common factor among the components of the composition of the inverse map and the original map
***********************************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        s = sourceInversionFactor(g)
  * Inputs:
      * g, a *note ring map: (Macaulay2Doc)RingMap,, a birational map $f : X
        \to Y$.
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Verbosity => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value 1, if 0
        then silence the function, if 1 then generate informative output which
        can be used to adjust strategies, if > 1 then generate a detailed
        description of the execution
      * CheckBirational => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,,
        default value false, whether to check birationality (if it is not
        birational, and CheckBirational is set to true, then an error will be
        thrown)
      * Strategy => a *note symbol: (Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,, default value
        HybridStrategy, choose the strategy to use: HybridStrategy,
        SimisStrategy, or ReesStrategy
      * HybridLimit => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value 15,
        within HybridStrategy, the option HybridLimit controls how often
        SimisStrategy and ReesStrategy are used, larger numbers means
        SimisStrategy will be executed longer
      * MinorsLimit => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value 0,
        how many submatrices of a variant of the Jacobian dual matrix to
        consider before switching to a different strategy
      * AssumeDominant => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,,
        default value false, whether to assume a rational map of schemes is
        dominant, if set to true it can speed up computation
      * QuickRank => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default
        value true, whether to compute rank via the package *note FastMinors:
        (FastMinors)Top,
  * Outputs:
      * s, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, an element of the
        coordinate ring of $X$ .

Description
===========

Given a map $f : X \to Y$, sourceInversionFactor computes the common factor
among the components of, $f^{(-1)}$ composed with $f$, which is an element of
the coordinate ring of $X$.

If AssumeDominant is set to true (default is false) then it assumes that the
rational map of projective varieties is dominant, otherwise the function will
compute the image by finding the kernel of $f$.

The Strategy option can be set to HybridStrategy (default), SimisStrategy,
ReesStrategy, or SaturationStrategy.  Note SimisStrategy will never terminate
for non-birational maps. If CheckBirational is set to false (default is true),
then no check for birationality will be done.  If it is set to true and the map
is not birational, then an error will be thrown if you are not using
SimisStrategy. The option HybridLimit controls HybridStrategy.  Larger values
of HybridLimit (the default value is 15) will mean that SimisStrategy is
executed longer, smaller values will mean that ReesStrategy will be switched to
sooner.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/7[x,y,z];                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : S = ZZ/7[a,b,c];                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : h = map(R, S, {y*z, x*z, x*y});                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : RingMap R <-- S                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : sourceInversionFactor h                                                 |
|sourceInversionFactor: About to find the image of the map.  If you know the i|
|        you may want to use the AssumeDominant option if this is slow.       |
|inverseOfMapSimis: About to find the image of the map.  If you know the image|
|        you may want to use the AssumeDominant option if this is slow.       |
|inverseOfMapSimis: About to check rank, if this is very slow, you may want to|
|inverseOfMapSimis: rank found, we computed enough of the Groebner basis.     |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = x*y*z                                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : R                                                                       |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|mage,                                                                        |
|                                                                             |
|,                                                                            |
|                                                                             |
| try turning QuickRank=>false.                                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
+---------------------------------------------+
|i5 : S=QQ[a,b,c,d];                          |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i6 : g=(b^2-a*c)*c*d;                        |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i7 : phi=map(S,S,transpose jacobian ideal g);|
|                                             |
|o7 : RingMap S <-- S                         |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i8 : sourceInversionFactor(phi, Verbosity=>0)|
|                                             |
|      2 4 2      5 2                         |
|o8 = b c d  - a*c d                          |
|                                             |
|o8 : S                                       |
+---------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

The current implementation of this function works only for irreducible
varieties..  Also see the function *note inverseMap: (Cremona)inverseMap, in
the package *note Cremona: (Cremona)Top,, which for some maps from projective
space is faster.  Additionally, also compare with the function *note
invertBirationalMap: (Parametrization)invertBirationalMap, of the package *note
Parametrization: (Parametrization)Top,.

See also
========

  * *note HybridStrategy: HybridStrategy, -- A strategy for determining whether
    a map is birational and computing its inverse
  * *note SimisStrategy: SimisStrategy, -- a strategy for determining whether a
    map is birational and computing its inverse
  * *note ReesStrategy: ReesStrategy, -- a strategy for determining whether a
    map is birational and computing its inverse

Ways to use sourceInversionFactor:
==================================

  * "sourceInversionFactor(RingMap)"

